# Chapter 5: change code in a running container
#
# Edit a Java file of service A, reload it into the RUNNING container (no restart, no new container), and see the new code
# answer. The service image carries HotswapAgent; `service.reload` compiles the module, copies only the changed classes in
# and waits until the agent has redefined them. Then a compile error, which changes nothing in the container. The chapter
# starts and ends with Api.java as git has it.
# @env local
# @var corr = {{correlation}}
# @var msg = ord-{{uuid}}

### shell clean-start
# Make sure Api.java is as committed (a run of this chapter that was interrupted could have left it edited).
# @cwd ..
git checkout -- estate/services/service-a/src/main/java/estate/a/Api.java

### shell container-before
# The id of A's container now, to compare after the reload. (Go templates like {{.Id}} are left alone: not a variable name.)
# @capture cid = out
podman inspect "deliberator-$DLB_WS-service-a" --format '{{.Id}}' | tr -d '\n'

### shell edit
# The edit you would make in the editor: line 57 of Api.java logs every ack.
# @cwd ..
# @assert out contains reloaded by the tour
sed -i 's/ACK received id=/ACK received (reloaded by the tour) id=/' estate/services/service-a/src/main/java/estate/a/Api.java
git diff -U0 estate/services/service-a/src/main/java/estate/a/Api.java

### op service.reload reload
# Compile, copy the changed class, redefine it in the running JVM. In the IDE: edit, save, tool window → Services → a → Reload.
# @assert $.mechanism == hotswap-agent
# @assert $.redefined contains estate.a.Api
{"name": "a"}

### sqs send queue/inbox send-order
# An order, to make A log an ack with the new code.
# @attr id={{msg}}
# @attr correlation={{corr}}
# @body ../estate/payloads/01-simple-order.json

### dynamodb get table/messages stored
# @until $.status.S == RECEIVED within 20s
{"Key": {"id": {"S": "{{msg}}"}}}

### http publish
# @assert status == 200
POST {{service/a}}/publish/{{msg}}
X-Correlation-Id: {{corr}}

### dynamodb get table/messages acked
# @until $.status.S == ACKED within 30s
{"Key": {"id": {"S": "{{msg}}"}}}

### op logs.fetch new-line
# A's log has the ack line of this order, written by the edited code.
# @assert $.lines == 1
{"target": "log/service-a", "since": "10m", "filter": "ACK received (reloaded by the tour) id={{msg}}"}

### shell container-after
# Same container as before the reload.
# @assert out == {{cid}}
podman inspect "deliberator-$DLB_WS-service-a" --format '{{.Id}}' | tr -d '\n'

### shell break-it
# Now a syntax error: the semicolon of line 57 removed.
# @cwd ..
sed -i '57s/;$//' estate/services/service-a/src/main/java/estate/a/Api.java

### op service.reload compile-error
# The compiler's error comes back as a typed error naming the file and line; nothing reached the container. The asserts make
# that error the expected outcome (without them an operation error fails the step).
# @assert ok == false
# @assert error.type == service/compile-failed
# @assert error.message contains Api.java:57
{"name": "a"}

### shell restore
# @cwd ..
git checkout -- estate/services/service-a/src/main/java/estate/a/Api.java

### op service.reload back
# The committed class back into the container.
# @assert $.redefined contains estate.a.Api
{"name": "a"}
